context recipe.","claim_id":"claim::formal_math_premise_retrieval","evidence_class":"algorithmic_projection","evidence_strength_rank":3,"organ_id":"formal_math_premise_retrieval","truth_accounting_bucket":"source_faithful_refactor","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.formal_math_premise_retrieval run --input fixtures/first_wave/formal_math_premise_retrieval/input --out receipts/first_wave/formal_math_premise_retrieval"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"59dcd28ace8ae81785d87e7b223731e8b19065e6ab3af2f8fd113e5477e6321c","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"algorithmic_projection","family":"formal_math_and_proof","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"source_faithful_refactor"},"component_id":"formal_math_premise_retrieval","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.formal_math_premise_retrieval","plain":"Proving a statement relies on earlier results, which must be found among many. It is given short public descriptions of known results, without proofs, and a query of keywords for what is to be proved. It scores each description by how many keywords it shares with the query, adds a bonus for a matching strategy tag, drops disallowed ones, and sorts from highest score to lowest. The result is a ranked shortlist, checked against the list the example expects, and inputs carrying a full proof are rejected. One small step, the scoring and sorting, is checked by a mathematical proof against written rules.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/formal_math_premise_retrieval.md","sha256":"2749324d4d16a20c1e4aab5792f2a6129dd0a040905c0a9ebb55323708ba5a24","text":"# Rank public premise metadata for a query\n\n> **In plain terms.** Proving a statement relies on earlier results, which must be found among many. It is given short public descriptions of known results, without proofs, and a query of keywords for what is to be proved. It scores each description by how many keywords it shares with the query, adds a bonus for a matching strategy tag, drops disallowed ones, and sorts from highest score to lowest. The result is a ranked shortlist, checked against the list the example expects, and inputs carrying a full proof are rejected. One small step, the scoring and sorting, is checked by a mathematical proof against written rules.\n\nThe retrieval fixture scores public Lean/Std premise metadata by token overlap with the query and adds a strategy-tag bonus. It filters candidates by allowed split, sorts by score and checks the shortlist against fixture expectations. The tests show that changing a premise can change the ranking and cause expected recall to fail.\n\nRanks public Lean/Std premise metadata by query-token overlap plus a strategy-tag bonus and checks the shortlist, rejecting a premise containing a proof body, a query carrying oracle premise IDs, test-split tuning, an unknown strategy and an over-budget context recipe.\n\n## Run the example\n\nPython 3.11 or later is required. From the repository root, use the Python API to direct both result and acceptance output into ignored local state. The CLI does not expose the acceptance path for this action.\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 - <<'PYCODE'\nfrom microcosm_core.organs.formal_math_premise_retrieval import run\nresult = run('fixtures/first_wave/formal_math_premise_retrieval/input', '.microcosm/component-guides/formal_math_premise_retrieval', acceptance_out='.microcosm/component-guides/formal_math_premise_retrieval/acceptance.json')\nprint(result['status'])\nPYCODE\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n`_score_query` calls the [proved premise-ranking core](../formal/components/premise_ranking/README.md). For normalized token counts it returns exactly the eligible occurrences, with scores equal to the sum of per-token minimum counts plus the strategy bonus. It orders them by descending score, premise-ID rank and original position. Python supplies tokenization and eligibility; the proof does not establish retrieval quality.\n\nThe example uses that core. `make component-replays` separately applies the shared [replay admission check](../formal/replay/README.md) to the exported bundle.\n\n## Source\n\n[Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/formal_math_premise_retrieval.py) · [Input](../fixtures/first_wave/formal_math_premise_retrieval/input) · [Tests](../tests/test_formal_math_premise_retrieval.py) · [Historical sample](../receipts/first_wave/formal_math_premise_retrieval/formal_math_premise_retrieval_result.json) · [JSON record](formal_math_premise_retrieval.json)\n\nFor research context on premise selection, see [this paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.03241).\n"},"proofs":[{"claim_ids":["claim::formal_math_premise_retrieval"],"component_ids":["formal_math_premise_retrieval"],"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"guide":{"availability":"available","plain":null,"plain_availability":"unrecorded","ref":"formal/components/premise_ranking/README.md","sha256":"fb7075762d2c98c663b1a977567d89b8deee0154c4c14554718aa80a67e900f3","text":"# Premise ranking core\n\n`PremiseRanking.dfy` supplies the executable core used by\n`formal_math_premise_retrieval._score_query`. For normalized query token counts\nand candidate rows, `Compute` returns exactly the eligible input occurrences.\nEach score is the sum of the minimum query and premise count for every token,\nplus one when the strategy matches. Results are sorted by descending score,\nascending premise-ID rank, then original position. The last key preserves\nPython's stable ordering when IDs and scores are equal.\n\nThe independent ghost specification constructs the expected multiset with\n`OverlapSpec` and states the lexicographic order with `RankBefore`; the executable\nuses a score loop and insertion sort. The contracts prove score equality,\noccurrence coverage and ordering for all finite inputs satisfying equal vector\nlengths. `negative/SplitFilterMutant.dfy` removes eligibility filtering and\nfails the coverage invariant.\n\nThe host is trusted to tokenize and count terms, derive split and strategy\nmembership, map Python's string ordering to ranks, and reconstruct field-hit\nmetadata. JSON conversion, worker isolation, generated runtime, Dafny, Boogie,\nZ3 and Python remain trusted. The proof says nothing about the usefulness of a\nretrieved premise or the correctness of the source metadata.\n\nThe metadata binds the proof source, mutant, pinned Dafny version and generated\nPython. The shared component-kernel checker reproves and regenerates these files;\nthe component tests exercise the production call and adversarial inputs.\n"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot","modeled_contracts":[{"assumptions":"Trusted host supplies normalized observations; adapter, isolated worker, Dafny, compiler and runtime remain trusted.","contract_sha256":"5aa8a9bea9fb4f10fce5d4560f0b63f6383248820c5d5249080705895b9a6d6e","descriptor_origin":"metadata_contract","entry_theorem_refs":["formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#Score","formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#Insert","formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#Compute"],"input_model":"Finite equal-length nonnegative token-count vectors and candidate eligibility, strategy and ID-rank observations.","limits":"Host tokenization, metadata, split and strategy checks are trusted; ranking usefulness is not proved.","requirements_review":{"status":"unrecorded"},"specification_refs":["formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#OverlapSpec","formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#ScoreSpec","formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#RankBefore","formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#Expected"],"statement":"Eligible candidate occurrences are scored by token-count overlap plus strategy bonus and sorted by score, ID rank and original position.","subclaim_id":"subclaim::premise_ranking"}],"proof":{"adapter_ref":"src/plectis/components/premise_ranking/_adapter.py","claim_ids":["claim::formal_math_premise_retrieval"],"component_ids":["formal_math_premise_retrieval"],"current_binding":{"assessment_time_basis":"index_generation_only","checker_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_kernels.py#check_binding","generated_python":{"PremiseRanking.py":"fbe9428bba9c4b363426395b36d4f005364c135ba6fa1b5409021059cdafb04e","System_/__init__.py":"96b6e33c036bc3aeab6d1810c7aef085184d09c407bdec032ea89d7a98843edf","__main__.py":"42c8f0f4781ec668b7774cac10e91dbcff60b256514bc594012c184637b7ad57","_dafny/__init__.py":"18d39decdedad0e188456e15d17f1dcd5113c4abc258ad6cb718e39534555e7a","module_.py":"bf65c0a05e9cef9deaf7a730ee722479189bdc03d5db1a2e13ad87d186eeb9d0"},"source_sha256":"85d9ae268927055a4ed2adef7b62d9253415398a22c7b22f2e1c242297592a97","status":"current_hash_binding_pass"},"entry_theorem_refs":["formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#Score","formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#Insert","formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#Compute"],"excerpts":[{"kind":"function","line_end":11,"line_start":6,"name":"OverlapSpec","ref":"formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#OverlapSpec","source_sha256":"85d9ae268927055a4ed2adef7b62d9253415398a22c7b22f2e1c242297592a97","text":"  ghost function OverlapSpec(q: seq<nat>, p: seq<nat>): nat\n    requires |q| == |p|\n    decreases |q|\n  {\n    if |q| == 0 then 0 else (if q[0] <= p[0] then q[0] else p[0]) + OverlapSpec(q[1..], p[1..])\n  }\n","text_sha256":"6f68b695620a5a0cb75227b3d9a0292c3de700bab7c4491609a8be83fc2ffd47"},{"kind":"function","line_end":14,"line_start":12,"name":"ScoreSpec","ref":"formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#ScoreSpec","source_sha256":"85d9ae268927055a4ed2adef7b62d9253415398a22c7b22f2e1c242297592a97","text":"  ghost function ScoreSpec(q: seq<nat>, c: Candidate): nat\n    requires |q| == |c.counts|\n  { OverlapSpec(q, c.counts) + (if c.bonus then 1 else 0) }\n","text_sha256":"7908f63916c4757f898d4bcf9d15a18efefa35b62f6214d040cc37f3f516b987"},{"kind":"predicate","line_end":23,"line_start":20,"name":"RankBefore","ref":"formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#RankBefore","source_sha256":"85d9ae268927055a4ed2adef7b62d9253415398a22c7b22f2e1c242297592a97","text":"  ghost predicate RankBefore(a: Entry, b: Entry) {\n    a.score >= b.score && (a.score != b.score ||\n      (a.idRank <= b.idRank && (a.idRank != b.idRank || a.index <= b.index)))\n  }\n","text_sha256":"6212425d3975ad076fdfd108c7b28fa7f0d142234440fb092e13739f58c564e4"},{"kind":"function","line_end":35,"line_start":27,"name":"Expected","ref":"formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#Expected","source_sha256":"85d9ae268927055a4ed2adef7b62d9253415398a22c7b22f2e1c242297592a97","text":"  ghost function Expected(q: seq<nat>, cs: seq<Candidate>, n: nat): multiset<Entry>\n    requires n <= |cs|\n    requires forall i :: 0 <= i < |cs| ==> |cs[i].counts| == |q|\n    decreases n\n  {\n    if n == 0 then multiset{} else\n      (Expected(q, cs, n-1) +\n        (if cs[n-1].eligible then multiset{Entry(n-1, cs[n-1].idRank, ScoreSpec(q, cs[n-1]))} else multiset{}))\n  }\n","text_sha256":"2377299c393ccb4c930fa860b779fc6fd11e3083eef27d55fd3c4ab7fa6ebf08"},{"kind":"method","line_end":50,"line_start":36,"name":"Score","ref":"formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#Score","source_sha256":"85d9ae268927055a4ed2adef7b62d9253415398a22c7b22f2e1c242297592a97","text":"  method Score(q: seq<nat>, p: seq<nat>, bonus: bool) returns (v: nat)\n    requires |q| == |p|\n    ensures v == OverlapSpec(q,p) + (if bonus then 1 else 0)\n  {\n    var i := |q|;\n    v := if bonus then 1 else 0;\n    while i > 0\n      invariant 0 <= i <= |q|\n      invariant v == OverlapSpec(q[i..],p[i..]) + (if bonus then 1 else 0)\n      decreases i\n    {\n      i := i - 1;\n      v := v + (if q[i] <= p[i] then q[i] else p[i]);\n    }\n  }\n","text_sha256":"3a6aa8be09d4b9aad357e3bcac68ad1495fb9f0c33faa45eb2e182bf68d1d8d9"},{"kind":"method","line_end":88,"line_start":51,"name":"Insert","ref":"formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#Insert","source_sha256":"85d9ae268927055a4ed2adef7b62d9253415398a22c7b22f2e1c242297592a97","text":"  method Insert(s: seq<Entry>, x: Entry) returns (t: seq<Entry>)\n    requires Ordered(s)\n    ensures Ordered(t)\n    ensures multiset(t) == multiset(s) + multiset{x}\n  {\n    var i := 0;\n    while i < |s| && !Before(x, s[i])\n      invariant 0 <= i <= |s|\n      invariant forall j :: 0 <= j < i ==> Before(s[j], x)\n      decreases |s| - i\n    {\n      assert Before(s[i], x);\n      i := i + 1;\n    }\n    t := s[..i] + [x] + s[i..];\n    assert s == s[..i] + s[i..];\n    assert multiset(t) == multiset(s[..i]) + multiset{x} + multiset(s[i..]);\n    assert forall j :: i <= j < |s| ==> Before(x, s[j]) by {\n      forall j | i <= j < |s| ensures Before(x, s[j]) {\n        if j > i { assert RankBefore(s[i], s[j]); }\n      }\n    }\n    assert Ordered(t) by {\n      forall j, k | 0 <= j < k < |t| ensures RankBefore(t[j], t[k]) {\n        if k < i {\n          assert t[j] == s[j] && t[k] == s[k];\n        } else if k == i {\n          assert t[j] == s[j] && t[k] == x;\n        } else if j == i {\n          assert t[j] == x && t[k] == s[k - 1];\n        } else if j < i {\n          assert t[j] == s[j] && t[k] == s[k - 1];\n        } else {\n          assert t[j] == s[j - 1] && t[k] == s[k - 1];\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n","text_sha256":"3a45fd5dee7129090cbf0a4c25e8b7ecef2105b004394539a703f26f3ba3b261"},{"kind":"method","line_end":108,"line_start":89,"name":"Compute","ref":"formal/components/premise_ranking/PremiseRanking.dfy#Compute","source_sha256":"85d9ae268927055a4ed2adef7b62d9253415398a22c7b22f2e1c242297592a97","text":"  method Compute(q: seq<nat>, cs: seq<Candidate>) returns (out: seq<Entry>)\n    requires forall i :: 0 <= i < |cs| ==> |cs[i].counts| == |q|\n    ensures Ordered(out)\n    ensures multiset(out) == Expected(q,cs,|cs|)\n  {\n    out := [];\n    var i := 0;\n    while i < |cs|\n      invariant 0 <= i <= |cs|\n      invariant Ordered(out)\n      invariant multiset(out) == Expected(q,cs,i)\n      decreases |cs| - i\n    {\n      if cs[i].eligible {\n        var v := Score(q,cs[i].counts,cs[i].bonus);\n        out := Insert(out, Entry(i,cs[i].idRank,v));\n      }\n      i := i + 1;\n    }\n  }\n","text_sha256":"7ae57f2a48958e22ad7e30966ee6815a6636c42196188dad4afa1703631a6193"}],"fresh_prover_result":{"status":"not_run_by_index"},"generated_refs":["src/plectis/components/premise_ranking/_generated/PremiseRanking.py","src/plectis/components/premise_ranking/_generated/System_/__init__.py","src/plectis/components/premise_ranking/_generated/__main__.py","src/plectis/components/premise_ranking/_generated/_dafny/__init__.py","src/plectis/components/premise_ranking/_generated/module_.py"],"guide":{"availability":"available","plain":null,"plain_availability":"unrecorded","ref":"formal/components/premise_ranking/README.md","sha256":"fb7075762d2c98c663b1a977567d89b8deee0154c4c14554718aa80a67e900f3","text":"# Premise ranking core\n\n`PremiseRanking.dfy` supplies the executable core used by\n`formal_math_premise_retrieval._score_query`. For normalized query token counts\nand candidate rows, `Compute` returns exactly the eligible input occurrences.\nEach score is the sum of the minimum query and premise count for every token,\nplus one when the strategy matches. Results are sorted by descending score,\nascending premise-ID rank, then original position. The last key preserves\nPython's stable ordering when IDs and scores are equal.\n\nThe independe